<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  task3_part1_approach.xml - Task 3, PART 1 of 2: the GPS approach, in GUIDED.
  Find the GREEN bay, commit to it, drive the lead-in and line-up legs, and
  STOP on the bay's centreline 3.0 m from its face, outside the fingers, bow in.
  task3_part2_dock_fire.xml (MANUAL) takes it from there: in to the firing
  spot on the camera and LiDAR, the docking report, the fire, the request.

  WHY TWO TREES. The approach is GUIDED setpoints (GPS); the dock and the shot
  are MANUAL stick overrides (this OmniX hull strafes only in MANUAL; GUIDED
  turns instead - docs/OPERATIONS.md). Between the two, SC goes from GUIDED to
  MANUAL. For practice that is the operator, and each part can be tested on its
  own.

  THE HANDOFF. A new goal (or a restarted bt_runner_node) forgets this part's
  dock book: which bay is which, and the committed bay. Part 2 cannot number
  three bays again from 3 m out (the outer faces are cut off at the image edge
  and never become tracks), so for practice the operator passes the bay on:
  this part logs "committed to bay N", part 2 is started with task3_bay N.

  FOR THE COMPETITION THE TWO MUST BECOME ONE RUN. A person moving SC, or
  typing in the bay, mid-run is an intervention. The way through is one tree
  with both parts, the dock book shared, and the mode change made by the tree
  on /crsd/set_mode (telemetry_bridge already takes it; the pilot's SC still
  outranks it). That needs a SetMode leaf and the team's sign-off on a tree
  that puts itself in MANUAL. Not done here.

  THE LEGS AND NUMBERS ARE task3_disruptive.xml's, unchanged (read its header
  for the why of each): looks from 5 m via a lead point, the strict GREEN + RED
  + RED rule before the lenient lone GREEN, the choice re-read on every leg
  (ChosenBaySafe), lead-in 5 m, line-up 3.0 m. The pool variant is
  task3_approach_test.xml (line-up 4.0 m, one look, dock_bays 1).

  PRECONDITIONS
    * GUIDED on SC; tree.sh true false task3_part1_approach.xml (the setpoints
      gate on; this tree never fires)
    * an approach point in the goal (go.sh with its "here" flag, the boat
      facing the dock) or the dock in view at the start
    * WP_RADIUS well under 1 m (0.2 - 0.3): at 2.0 ArduRover parks 2 m short
      of every point (task3_disruptive.xml point 5). Set it back afterwards.
    * dock_bays = the bays actually there (3 on the course, 1 at the pool)

  WHEN IT ENDS (SUCCESS) the boat loiters at the line-up point in GUIDED. The
  log names the bay: "committed to bay N".
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="Task3Part1Approach">
  <BehaviorTree ID="Task3Part1Approach">
    <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

      <IsAutonomous/>
      <DockCameraAlive max_age_s="3.0"/>
      <UpdateDockBook/>

      <Sequence name="approach">

        <SetTask token="TASK_COORDINATED_LOGISTICS"/>

        <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="3" name="dock_attempts">
          <Sequence name="find_and_line_up">

            <ReactiveFallback name="find_safe_bay">
              <SafeBayKnown need_others_red="true"/>
              <RetryUntilSuccessful num_attempts="4" name="looks">
                <Sequence name="look">
                  <PickVantage standoff="5.0" lead_m="2.0" out="{vantage}" lead="{lead}"/>
                  <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{lead}" tolerance="1.0"/>
                  <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{vantage}" tolerance="1.0"/>
                  <!-- watch, then fail the look so the retry moves on; readings
                       pile up meanwhile and SafeBayKnown above ends it early -->
                  <ForceFailure>
                    <Sleep msec="12000"/>
                  </ForceFailure>
                </Sequence>
              </RetryUntilSuccessful>
              <SafeBayKnown need_others_red="false"/>
            </ReactiveFallback>

            <CommitSafeBay/>

            <Fallback name="lead_in">
              <LinedUp min_along_m="2.7" lateral_tol="0.4" heading_tol_deg="20.0"/>
              <ReactiveSequence name="to_lead">
                <ChosenBaySafe min_ema="0.3"/>
                <DockWaypoint point="lead" predock_m="3.0" berth_m="1.25" lead_m="2.0" out="{goal}"/>
                <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="1.0"/>
              </ReactiveSequence>
            </Fallback>
            <ReactiveSequence name="line_up">
              <ChosenBaySafe min_ema="0.3"/>
              <DockWaypoint point="predock" predock_m="3.0" berth_m="1.25" lead_m="2.0" out="{goal}"/>
              <NavigateTo target="port" goal="{goal}" tolerance="0.4" resend_m="0.2"/>
            </ReactiveSequence>

          </Sequence>
        </RetryUntilSuccessful>

      </Sequence>
    </ReactiveSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
